From fba82c68960cc58eba0638aa7a1e320a1cb0a1d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:54:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "Remove ION sepolicy"

This reverts commit 9b2d37dc2 (Remove ION sepolicy).

Legacy devices such as exynos8890 (herolte) still allocate every
graphics, camera and codec buffer through /dev/ion. Without the
/dev/ion label and the ion_device rules, /dev/ion falls back to the
generic "device" type and every ION user is denied once SELinux is
enforcing (e.g. the camera HAL fails all buffer allocations).

Conflicts resolved: dropped the TODO(482058879) comments on the
retained ion_device/sysfs_ion types and kept the current compat
mapping header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Iaa44e6c26ca78b521abfe7c755a921ac565bd834
